{%- comment -%}
  DotAim customizations that have no theme setting to express them.

  Kept in this snippet, rendered from layout/theme.liquid immediately after
  'css-variables', so that stock theme files stay unforked and a Be Yours
  update only ever conflicts on the single render line in theme.liquid.

  Ported from Lush KSA (lush.sa.com), which instead edited snippets/
  css-variables.liquid directly. Deliberately NOT ported: KSA's 'SAR'
  riyal-symbol font and .sar_symbol rule, which are Saudi-only. Qatar is QAR.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- style -%}
  /* Lush brand heading face. Held in the theme's own assets rather than the
     store's Files, so it is versioned in git, travels with the theme, and
     cannot be broken by someone deleting a file in the admin. */
  @font-face {
    font-family: 'LushHandwritten_Bd';
    src: url('{{ 'LushHandwritten_Bd.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2'),
         url('{{ 'LushHandwritten_Bd.woff' | asset_url }}') format('woff');
    font-weight: normal;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  :root {
    /* The brand face as its own variable, so it can be applied to specific
       elements independently of what the heading font happens to be. Lush
       UK/HQ and Lush Lebanon use this face for headlines only, not for
       prices and UI text -- see the note in docs/theme-porting-list.md. */
    --font-lush-handwritten: 'LushHandwritten_Bd', var(--font-body-family);

  }

  /* Where the brand face is applied.

     Matches lushlebanon.com rather than KSA: Lebanon leaves the heading font
     as the theme setting and applies the handwritten face only to display
     type -- product headings, card text and slideshow headings -- which is
     how Lush UK/HQ treat it. KSA instead forces it on every heading, prices
     and UI text included.

     The .font-lush-handwritten utility is there so any other element can opt
     in from the theme editor's per-section custom CSS, which is what Lebanon
     does for selected image-with-text headings. */
  .font-lush-handwritten,
  .product__heading,
  .card-information__text,
  .slideshow__heading {
    font-family: var(--font-lush-handwritten);
  }

  /* Arabic is cursive: its letters join. The theme applies letter-spacing in
     15 places in base.css (up to 0.3rem) and rtl.css does not reset it, which
     visually severs those joins. Ported from KSA, where it is the one Arabic
     typography fix they carried. */
  html[lang='ar'] * {
    letter-spacing: 0 !important;
  }
{%- endstyle -%}
